  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given two integer sequences A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ and B1,B2,…,BMB_1, B_2, \\ldots, B_MB1​,B2​,…,BM​. For any two sequences U1,U2,…,UpU_1, U_2, \\ldots, U_pU1​,U2​,…,Up​ and V1,V2,…,VqV_1, V_2, \\ldots, V_qV1​,V2​,…,Vq​, we define\nScore(U,V)=∑i=1p∑j=1qUi⋅Vj .Score(U, V) = \\sum_{i=1}^p \\sum_{j=1}^q  U_i \\cdot V_j \\,.Score(U,V)=∑i=1p​∑j=1q​Ui​⋅Vj​.\n\nYou should process QQQ queries of three types:\n\n\n111 LLL RRR XXX: Add XXX to each of the elements AL,AL+1,…,ARA_L, A_{L+1}, \\ldots, A_RAL​,AL+1​,…,AR​.\n222 LLL RRR XXX: Add XXX to each of the elements BL,BL+1,…,BRB_L, B_{L+1}, \\ldots, B_RBL​,BL+1​,…,BR​.\n333: Print Score(A,B)Score(A, B)Score(A,B) modulo 998,244,353998,244,353998,244,353.\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains two integers, NNN and MMM, denoting the length of AAA and BBB respectively.\nThe second line contains NNN integers, elements of AAA.\nThe third line contains MMM integers, elements of BBB.\nThe next line will contain an integer, QQQ, number of queries.\nEach of the next QQQ lines will contain one of 333 kinds of updates as mentioned in the statement.\n\nIt’s guaranteed that each update is a valid update operation.\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each query of the third type, print a single line containing one integer - the answer to that query.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤101 \\le T \\le 101≤T≤10",
      "2≤N,M,Q≤1052 \\le N, M, Q \\le 10^52≤N,M,Q≤105",
